        card("Activity 4: switch may/me and mayroon/meron (the book’s key)", "Add linkers where needed: meron needs the linker (ba bang, ka bang), may does not.", tables=[table(["Sentence", "Rewritten"], [list(r) for r in _RW], say=[0, 1])]),
        card("Activity 5: um and mag verbs found in the presentations (the book’s key)", "The book’s chart gives the infinitive, past, present and future: for magschedule it prints nag-ii-schedule and mag-iischedule.", tables=[table(["Infinitive", "Meaning", "Past", "Present", "Future"], [list(r) for r in _CVR] + [["magschedule", "to schedule", "nagschedule", "nag-ii-schedule", "mag-iischedule"]], say=[0, 2, 3, 4])]),
        card("Notes on the chart", "Meron and me are colloquial forms of mayroon and may. Tawagan (to call on the phone) and palitan (to exchange) are -an/han/nan verbs taken up in later lessons."),
